  Wands of cancellation are useful against them as they have MR of 0.
Ditto sea monsters.  Elbereth is easier and safer with an athame, wand
of lightning/fire.  Spells of scare/charm monster are safer as well.
Spell of cancellation is infinitely superior to /oCanc.

  Monsters with non-zero MR can silently resist.  Floating eyes are one
deadly example. (Yes, posters have told of dying to floating eyes as a
result of this.)

  Werecreatures are useful to cancel, but can silently resist.
Fortunately their intrinsic MR is rather low.  A double zap should be a
sure thing.

  The first time you successfully cancel a mind flayer you will get an
unpleasant surprise.

  Yes, wands of cancellation have uses, but nothing that can't be done
more safely using other methods.   The risk/reward ratio seems much to
high to me.  (Stanley Myrick might say the same.)


  Even with all that, I have in the past recommended carrying a wand of
cancellation for use against sea monsters that have enwrapped you.
Carrying the wand without carrying a BoH might be an even better
solution.


  (At least one poster accidentally broke their wand of cancellation
while preparing to exit the dungeon with the Amulet of Yendor.  It
wasn't much of an improvement over exploding their BoH.)




